s, and deliverables of the project are established.\"},\"target\":null,\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"The 'Design Database Schema' activity is permitted to occur only if a 'Develop Frontend Interface' activity has occurred before it within the same process instance.\",\"template\":\"Precedence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Design Database Schema\",\"description\":\"The 'Design Database Schema' activity involves creating the structural design of the database, including tables, relationships, and constraints to support the application's data requirements.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Develop Frontend Interface\",\"description\":\"The 'Develop Frontend Interface' activity encompasses building the user-facing components of the application, ensuring an intuitive and responsive user experience.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"If an 'Integrate Payment Gateway' activity occurs, then an 'Implement Backend Logic' activity must eventually occur after the 'Integrate Payment Gateway' event at some point in the same process instance. There is no requirement on how soon or what events may occur in between. Multiple 'Integrate Payment Gateway' events can be pending at the same time, and a single 'Implement Backend Logic' can fulfill the obligation for all preceding 'Integrate Payment Gateway' events. If 'Integrate Payment Gateway' does not occur, the constraint imposes no obligation on the occurrence of 'Implement Backend Logic'.\",\"template\":\"Response\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Integrate Payment Gateway\",\"description\":\"The 'Integrate Payment Gateway' activity involves connecting the application to a third-party payment processing service to enable financial transactions.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Implement Backend Logic\",\"description\":\"The 'Implement Backend Logic' activity involves coding the server-side functionality of the application, including business rules, data processing, and API development.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"If 'Test System Functionality' activity occurs, then 'Deploy Application to Server' must also occur in the same process instance, and vice-versa. The events can occur multiple times and in any order relative to each other. If neither event occurs, the constraint is still considered satisfied.\",\"template\":\"Co-Existence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Test System Functionality\",\"description\":\"The 'Test System Functionality' activity includes executing various tests on the system to verify that all components work as expected and meet the specified requirements.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Deploy Application to Server\",\"description\":\"The 'Deploy Application to Server' activity involves transferring the application from a development environment to a live server environment where it becomes accessible to end users.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"A 'Deploy Application to Server' activity must be followed by a 'Monitor System Performance' activity at some point later in the same process instance. Conversely, a 'Monitor System Performance' event can occur only if a 'Deploy Application to Server' event has occurred before it within the same process instance. This bidirectional and ordered dependency ensures that 'Deploy Application to Server' imposes obligations for future 'Monitor System Performance', and 'Monitor System Performance' cannot occur without prior 'Deploy Application to Server'. Multiple 'Deploy Application to Server' and 'Monitor System Performance' are allowed, with each 'Deploy Application to Server' eventually leading to a 'Monitor System Performance' and each 'Monitor System Performance' being justified by a preceding 'Deploy Application to Server'.\",\"template\":\"Succession\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Deploy Application to Server\",\"description\":\"The 'Deploy Application to Server' activity involves transferring the application from a development environment to a live server environment where it becomes accessible to end users.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Monitor System Performance\",\"description\":\"The 'Monitor System Performance' activity encompasses tracking and analyzing the application's operational metrics, such as response times, resource usage, and uptime, to ensure optimal performance.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"A 'Gather User Feedback' activity cannot be preceded by a 'Define Project Scope' activity within the same process instance. This means that if any 'Define Project Scope' event has occurred before a 'Gather User Feedback' event in the process instance, then that 'Gather User Feedback' is disallowed. Multiple 'Gather User Feedback' and 'Define Project Scope' events can occur, but all instances of 'Gather User Feedback' must occur before any instance of 'Define Project Scope'.\",\"template\":\"Not Precedence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Gather User Feedback\",\"description\":\"The 'Gather User Feedback' activity involves collecting opinions, suggestions, and issue reports from users regarding their experience with the application.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Define Project Scope\",\"description\":\"The 'Define Project Scope' activity represents the initial phase of a project where the boundaries, objectives, and deliverables of the project are established.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"The 'Define Project Scope' activity must not be fo